   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Letters that make up blocks",
     "texto": [
      "Hangul is an **alphabet**: the letters are grouped into **syllable blocks**, not written all in a row.",
      "가 = ㄱ + ㅏ; 나 = ㄴ + ㅏ.",
      "Vertical vowels go to the **right** of the consonant: 가, 거, 기. Horizontal vowels go **underneath**: 고, 구, 그.",
      "If a syllable begins with a vowel sound, ㅇ is written in front as a spelling placeholder: 아. In that position it does not represent a consonant."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Six vowels",
     "texto": [
      "ㅏ, ㅣ, ㅗ and ㅜ can be approximated with English vowels, although their length and quality depend on the speaker.",
      "ㅓ does not match any English vowel exactly: **ŏ** is a reading aid, not a phonetic transcription.",
      "ㅡ does not have an exact equivalent either: it is pronounced with the lips not rounded; **ŭ** is only a support convention."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
